 "lines": [
  {
   "say": "Fewer cars. Worse traffic. How?",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "Israel has four hundred and four vehicles for every thousand people.",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "America has more than twice that. Germany and the Netherlands, about six hundred.",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "So Israelis own fewer cars. Now look at the roads.",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "Vehicles per kilometre of road: Israel, two thousand seven hundred. The OECD average: under eight hundred.",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "Three and a half times more crowded.",
   "screen": "*3.5x* the OECD average",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "How? A tiny country, and a population that doubled since 1990.",
   "screen": "Population: *doubled* since 1990",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "Plus the highest birth rate in the OECD: about three kids per woman.",
   "screen": "*2.9* kids per woman: top of the OECD",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "Now send them all to work in Tel Aviv.",
   "screen": "Everyone to *Tel Aviv*",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "Evening rush hour on the Ayalon highway: fourteen kilometres an hour.",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "That's bicycle speed.",
   "screen": "That's *bicycle* speed 🚲",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "The fix has started. The Red Line light rail opened in 2023, and two more lines are being built.",
   "screen": "Red Line: *2023.* Two more lines coming",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "So, train or car? Which would you take?",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "If you love Israeli facts, follow Noam Roz for more.",
   "wav": "ref/follow_line_noam.wav",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "Until then: fewer cars, worse traffic.",
   "gap": 0.1
  }
 ],
